{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-matching/third-reader-packet.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"dispute\": 1,\n  \"opened_question\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will China's government allow selected Chinese AI firms (including Alibaba Group Holding) to buy Nvidia H200 GPUs, and at what scale, replacing the current restriction that bars Chinese firms from purchasing the device?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Beijing implements its reported plan to permit selected Chinese companies to buy limited numbers of Nvidia H200 GPUs, the scale of permitted purchases, and any subsequent broadening or tightening versus the current restriction.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal year ending late January 2027 (reported ~February 2027); set as the current fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision, because the item gives no date for Beijing's authorisation.\"\n  },\n  \"reference_question\": \"q08\"\n },\n {\n  \"dispute\": 2,\n  \"opened_question\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will DRAM/HBM contract prices remain elevated through calendar 2027, extending the shortage that has raised GPU makers' memory input costs?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Direction and level of DRAM/HBM contract prices through calendar 2027, specifically whether they remain above 2026 levels or normalize as Micron's 2027/2028 outlook suggests.\",\n   \"period\": \"Full-year calendar 2027; checked against Q4 2027 DRAM contract price releases (TrendForce/DRAMeXchange) and memory makers' Q4 2027 results, reported roughly January 2028.\"\n  },\n  \"reference_question\": \"q05\"\n },\n {\n  \"dispute\": 3,\n  \"opened_question\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will Nvidia launch its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by 2028-12-31?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 rack architecture launches by the end of 2028.\",\n   \"period\": \"year 2028; due 2028-12-31\"\n  },\n  \"reference_question\": \"q18\"\n },\n {\n  \"dispute\": 4,\n  \"opened_question\": {\n   \"description\": \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue growth be in FY2027?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA total revenue growth in FY2027\",\n   \"period\": \"year FY2027; due 2027-02-28\"\n  },\n  \"reference_question\": \"q01\"\n },\n {\n  \"dispute\": 5,\n  \"opened_question\": {\n   \"description\": \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue growth be in FY2028?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA total revenue growth in FY2028\",\n   \"period\": \"year FY2028; due 2028-02-29\"\n  },\n  \"reference_question\": \"q22\"\n },\n {\n  \"dispute\": 6,\n  \"opened_question\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Kyber NVL144 AI server rack by December 31, 2028?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 AI server rack begins shipping by the end of 2028.\",\n   \"period\": \"year 2028; due 2028-12-31\"\n  },\n  \"reference_question\": \"q18\"\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-matching/adjudication-earlier-rulings.md'","aggregated_output":"# Adjudication of the four identity disagreements (third blind reader, 2026-11-10)\n\n**All four are SAME:**\n- **dev-d2 clean-1 and dev-d3 clean-1, against q09.**\n  - D248 boundary 1, with R2-e naming the credit-support programme of the financing-commitments total as such a merge.\n  - It is checked in the same FY2027 10-K.\n  - Every must-open entry q09 covers uses this credit-support wording.\n- **dev-d3 clean-3, against q08.**\n  - The same Chinese permission settles \"sell to commercial customers\" and \"import\" (R2-f).\n  - The deadline is the same, and \"(and other U.S.-approved)\" is wording.\n- **dev-d3 clean-5, against q18.**\n  - Boundary 2: a 2028-or-later first shipment is q18's no.\n  - Boundary 3: NVL576 is a later configuration of the same generation (D259 files the NVL576 delay under the Kyber question).\n\n**The general rule stated by the reader** is copied into MATCHING.md §1.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/questions-v1.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n \"ruler_version\": 1,\n \"about\": \"22 seed questions (poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json) + the one must_open bet no seed covers; must_open gists mapped by bet (D248)\",\n \"seeds_sha256\": \"fca16f42dd7153e852c42527883552b86567f33d7e1ed3c11ef600c8a37037d6\",\n \"gold_sha256\": \"6f9476bb6a81ea590af273a71565e7c3c0f49908d26274b8482d52cfdee31a21\",\n \"questions\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q01\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v1\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q02\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v2\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $440 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 440000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least $360 billion and below $440 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 360000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 440000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least $310 billion and below $360 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 310000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 360000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least $260 billion and below $310 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 260000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 310000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below $260 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 260000000000.0\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q03\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v3\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What non-GAAP gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"unit\": \"percent (75 means 75%)\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is at least 77%.\",\n     \"lo\": 77.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is at least 75% but below 77%.\",\n     \"lo\": 75.0,\n     \"hi\": 77.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is at least 73% but below 75%, compared with the article's 75% reference level.\",\n     \"lo\": 73.0,\n     \"hi\": 75.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is at least 71% but below 73%.\",\n     \"lo\": 71.0,\n     \"hi\": 73.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is below 71%.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 71.0\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q04\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v4\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $550 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $550 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 550000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$550 billion to below $600 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $550 billion and less than $600 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 550000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 600000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$600 billion to below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $600 billion and less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 600000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": [\n    {\n     \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n     \"input_id\": \"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e\",\n     \"gist\": \"Combined calendar-2026 data-center capital expenditure of the 'big four' AI hyperscalers: five rungs around the ~$650bn plan (e.g. below $600bn / $600-640bn / $640-680bn / $680-750bn / above $750bn); due when the last of the four publishes calendar-2026 capex\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n     \"input_id\": \"gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c\",\n     \"gist\": \"Combined calendar-2026 data-center capital expenditure of the 'big four' AI hyperscalers: five rungs around the ~$650bn plan (e.g. below $600bn / $600-640bn / $640-680bn / $680-750bn / above $750bn); due when the last of the four publishes calendar-2026 capex\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q05\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v5\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\",\n   \"question\": \"How will server DRAM and HBM contract prices in calendar 2027 compare with calendar 2026?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-01-31\",\n   \"unit\": \"percent change 2027 vs 2026 (10 means up 10%)\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Up 30% or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"2027 average contract prices at least 30% above 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": 30,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Up 10% to 30%\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least 10% and below 30% above 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": 10,\n     \"hi\": 30\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Flat\",\n     \"condition\": \"within 10% of 2026 either way.\",\n     \"lo\": -10,\n     \"hi\": 10\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Down 10% to 30%\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least 10% and below 30% under 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": -30,\n     \"hi\": -10\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Down 30% or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"30% or more under 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": -30\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": [\n    {\n     \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n     \"input_id\": \"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e\",\n     \"gist\": \"Change in DRAM (including HBM) contract prices in calendar 2027 versus calendar 2026: five rungs (falls / flat within ±5% / rises 5-20% / rises 20-50% / rises more than 50%)\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q06\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v6\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What share of calendar-2026 data-center AI accelerator spending will NVIDIA hold, by the first published full-year estimate?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n   \"unit\": \"percent\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"share at least 85%.\",\n     \"lo\": 85,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least 78% and below 85%.\",\n     \"lo\": 78,\n     \"hi\": 85\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least 70% and below 78%.\",\n     \"lo\": 70,\n     \"hi\": 78\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least 60% and below 70%.\",\n     \"lo\": 60,\n     \"hi\": 70\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 60%.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 60\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q07\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v7\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q08\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v8\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\",\n   \"question\": \"Will Chinese authorities issue any authorization for Chinese companies to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"Chinese authorities publicly authorize at least one Chinese company to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Chinese authorities have not publicly authorized any Chinese company to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": [\n    {\n     \"day\": \"2026-07-08\",\n     \"input_id\": \"gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c\",\n     \"gist\": \"Will Chinese authorities formally permit Chinese AI companies to buy (import) NVIDIA H200 chips by 2027-01-31? Two rungs; the article gives no date, so the due date is NVIDIA's FY2027 year-end, a researcher-set check date; the authority is the Chinese government\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n     \"input_id\": \"gnews:50a84fa6b2f3eb33f29948a4\",\n     \"gist\": \"Will China formally permit its top AI firms (Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek) to buy NVIDIA H200 chips by 2027-01-31 (NVIDIA's FY2027 year-end; the article gives no date, so this is a researcher-set check date)?\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q09\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v9\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What total amount of financing commitments and capacity backstops to customers and partners will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is below $5 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 5000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is at least $5 billion and below $10 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 5000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 10000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is at least $10 billion and below $20 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 10000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 20000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is at least $20 billion and below $40 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 20000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 40000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is at least $40 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 40000000000.0,\n 